{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.121058205d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-303","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Valewood Museum is in central Spain. It opened in 1956.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 346,281 visitors.</li><li>The Ironwood Museum is in northern Chile. It opened in 1948.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 188,117 visitors.</li><li>Both are art museums with free admission.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two museums.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Valewood Museum is in central Spain, and the Ironwood Museum is in northern Chile.","The Valewood Museum, which is in central Spain, is one of several art museums with free admission.","The annual attendance of the Valewood Museum (346,281 visitors) is greater than that of the Ironwood Museum (188,117 visitors).","The Valewood Museum opened in 1956, while the Ironwood Museum opened in 1948."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.bf06148aeb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-306","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Thornbury is in central Canada. It was first surveyed in 2010.</li><li>Its surface area is 352 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Wexford is in northern Chile. It was first surveyed in 1954.</li><li>Its surface area is 308 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are reservoirs created by dams.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two lakes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The surface area of Lake Thornbury (352 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Wexford (308 square kilometers).","Lake Thornbury is in central Canada, and Lake Wexford is in northern Chile.","Lake Thornbury was first surveyed in 2010, while Lake Wexford was first surveyed in 1954.","Lake Thornbury, which is in central Canada, is one of several reservoirs created by dams."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.27da489b1b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-311","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Sable Museum is in eastern Poland. It opened in 1992.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 761,394 visitors.</li><li>The Kingsley Museum is in western Scotland. It opened in 1896.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 342,875 visitors.</li><li>Both are museums of natural history.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two museums.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Sable Museum opened in 1992, while the Kingsley Museum opened in 1896.","The Sable Museum is in eastern Poland, and the Kingsley Museum is in western Scotland.","The annual attendance of the Sable Museum (761,394 visitors) is greater than that of the Kingsley Museum (342,875 visitors).","The Sable Museum, which is in eastern Poland, is one of several museums of natural history."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.792ed71ec6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-322","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Valewood Tunnel is in eastern Poland. It opened in 1953.</li><li>Its length is 32 kilometers.</li><li>The Kingsley Tunnel is in southern Brazil. It opened in 1933.</li><li>Its length is 22 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Valewood Tunnel is in eastern Poland, and the Kingsley Tunnel is in southern Brazil.","The length of the Valewood Tunnel (32 kilometers) is greater than that of the Kingsley Tunnel (22 kilometers).","The Valewood Tunnel opened in 1953, while the Kingsley Tunnel opened in 1933.","The Valewood Tunnel, which is in eastern Poland, is one of several tunnels that pass under a mountain range."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.394267724d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-323","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Valewood National Park is in southern Brazil. It was established in 1894.</li><li>Its area is 6,025 square kilometers.</li><li>Fenwick National Park is in eastern Poland. It was established in 1998.</li><li>Its area is 5,087 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks that protect coastal wetlands.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two parks.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The area of Valewood National Park (6,025 square kilometers) is greater than that of Fenwick National Park (5,087 square kilometers).","Valewood National Park, which is in southern Brazil, is one of several parks that protect coastal wetlands.","Valewood National Park is in southern Brazil, and Fenwick National Park is in eastern Poland.","Valewood National Park was established in 1894, while Fenwick National Park was established in 1998."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.0f55827ae4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-326","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Cresthill Bridge is in central Canada. It opened in 1983.</li><li>Its main span is 1,001 meters.</li><li>The Sable Bridge is in southern Norway. It opened in 1975.</li><li>Its main span is 987 meters.</li><li>Both are suspension bridges.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two bridges.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Cresthill Bridge is in central Canada, and the Sable Bridge is in southern Norway.","The main span of the Cresthill Bridge (1,001 meters) is greater than that of the Sable Bridge (987 meters).","The Cresthill Bridge opened in 1983, while the Sable Bridge opened in 1975.","The Cresthill Bridge, which is in central Canada, is one of several suspension bridges."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b5db200d0b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-328","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Museum is in eastern Poland. It opened in 1995.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 381,506 visitors.</li><li>The Brookhaven Museum is in western Scotland. It opened in 1911.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 295,790 visitors.</li><li>Both are museums of natural history.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two museums.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The annual attendance of the Glenrock Museum (381,506 visitors) is greater than that of the Brookhaven Museum (295,790 visitors).","The Glenrock Museum, which is in eastern Poland, is one of several museums of natural history.","The Glenrock Museum opened in 1995, while the Brookhaven Museum opened in 1911.","The Glenrock Museum is in eastern Poland, and the Brookhaven Museum is in western Scotland."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.5908a38c05","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-336","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mount Juniper is in western Kenya. It was first climbed in 1892.</li><li>Its height is 6,115 meters.</li><li>Mount Cresthill is in eastern Australia. It was first climbed in 1964.</li><li>Its height is 5,586 meters.</li><li>Both are peaks in the same mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two mountains.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mount Juniper was first climbed in 1892, while Mount Cresthill was first climbed in 1964.","Mount Juniper is in western Kenya, and Mount Cresthill is in eastern Australia.","Mount Juniper, which is in western Kenya, is one of several peaks in the same mountain range.","The height of Mount Juniper (6,115 meters) is greater than that of Mount Cresthill (5,586 meters)."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.aebc6d1c03","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-337","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Yarrow Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1893.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 11 meters.</li><li>The Fenwick Observatory is in eastern Australia. It began operating in 1902.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 8 meters.</li><li>Both are radio observatories.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Yarrow Observatory began operating in 1893, while the Fenwick Observatory began operating in 1902.","The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Yarrow Observatory (11 meters) is greater than that of the Fenwick Observatory (8 meters).","The Yarrow Observatory, which is in southern New Zealand, is one of several radio observatories.","The Yarrow Observatory is in southern New Zealand, and the Fenwick Observatory is in eastern Australia."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.eff80b2b38","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-342","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Kingsley Museum is in southern New Zealand. It opened in 1959.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 266,405 visitors.</li><li>The Halden Museum is in eastern Australia. It opened in 2010.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 241,101 visitors.</li><li>Both are art museums with free admission.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two museums.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Kingsley Museum is in southern New Zealand, and the Halden Museum is in eastern Australia.","The annual attendance of the Kingsley Museum (266,405 visitors) is greater than that of the Halden Museum (241,101 visitors).","The Kingsley Museum, which is in southern New Zealand, is one of several art museums with free admission.","The Kingsley Museum opened in 1959, while the Halden Museum opened in 2010."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.5903b0e7d7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-360","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mount Redfern is in southern Brazil. It was first climbed in 1986.</li><li>Its height is 5,889 meters.</li><li>Mount Kingsley is in central Canada. It was first climbed in 1937.</li><li>Its height is 2,772 meters.</li><li>Both are dormant volcanoes.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two mountains.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The height of Mount Redfern (5,889 meters) is greater than that of Mount Kingsley (2,772 meters).","Mount Redfern, which is in southern Brazil, is one of several dormant volcanoes.","Mount Redfern is in southern Brazil, and Mount Kingsley is in central Canada.","Mount Redfern was first climbed in 1986, while Mount Kingsley was first climbed in 1937."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.8d551bb739","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-368","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Quarry Tunnel is in eastern Australia. It opened in 1893.</li><li>Its length is 17 kilometers.</li><li>The Cresthill Tunnel is in northern Chile. It opened in 1917.</li><li>Its length is 5 kilometers.</li><li>Both are railway tunnels.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Quarry Tunnel opened in 1893, while the Cresthill Tunnel opened in 1917.","The length of the Quarry Tunnel (17 kilometers) is greater than that of the Cresthill Tunnel (5 kilometers).","The Quarry Tunnel, which is in eastern Australia, is one of several railway tunnels.","The Quarry Tunnel is in eastern Australia, and the Cresthill Tunnel is in northern Chile."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.51273e6e12","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-379","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Pembrook Museum is in western Kenya. It opened in 1930.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 864,230 visitors.</li><li>The Redfern Museum is in southern Norway. It opened in 1994.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 703,803 visitors.</li><li>Both are museums of natural history.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two museums.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Pembrook Museum opened in 1930, while the Redfern Museum opened in 1994.","The annual attendance of the Pembrook Museum (864,230 visitors) is greater than that of the Redfern Museum (703,803 visitors).","The Pembrook Museum, which is in western Kenya, is one of several museums of natural history.","The Pembrook Museum is in western Kenya, and the Redfern Museum is in southern Norway."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.0f1c656ac6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-10","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Iyer is an ecologist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Iyer compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Iyer found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Iyer concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Iyer found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Iyer concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","Because robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier, Iyer concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","To investigate the question, Iyer compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.8014d75855","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-26","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Moreau is a materials scientist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Because coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer, Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","To investigate the question, Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7f5b80c971","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-27","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Moreau is a materials scientist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer, Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","To investigate the question, Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.dccef22308","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-38","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Solberg is a sociologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Solberg surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Solberg found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Solberg concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Solberg surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Solberg concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Solberg found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","Because residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened, Solberg concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.4b60a6d220","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-42","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Kowalski is a geologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Kowalski measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Kowalski found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because bare slopes lost several times more soil, Kowalski concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","To investigate the question, Kowalski measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.","Kowalski found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.","Kowalski concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.8ab1fae15c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-50","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Delacroix is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Delacroix asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Delacroix found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days, Delacroix concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","To investigate the question, Delacroix asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.","Delacroix concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","Delacroix found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.405ac138b5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-55","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Castellano is a zoologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Castellano gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Castellano found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Castellano concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Castellano gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Because elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day, Castellano concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Castellano concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Castellano found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.640de513a5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-68","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Moreau is a linguist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Moreau gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Moreau found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Moreau concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors, Moreau concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","To investigate the question, Moreau gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Moreau found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.","Moreau concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.55557664d9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-72","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Abara is an economist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Abara tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Abara found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Abara concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Abara found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","To investigate the question, Abara tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Because output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly, Abara concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.f2fcaf4c08","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-90","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Varga is a hydrologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Varga compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Varga found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Varga concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","To investigate the question, Varga compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Because river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands, Varga concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","Varga concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.440d375abe","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-98","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Mensah is an education researcher.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Mensah had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Mensah found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Mensah concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Mensah had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Mensah concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Because children in the read-aloud group learned more new words, Mensah concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Mensah found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.581ad59440","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-119","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Delacroix is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Delacroix asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Delacroix found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Delacroix asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Delacroix concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Because tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep, Delacroix concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Delacroix found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.ec74969920","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-123","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Ferreira is an ornithologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings, Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b6acd459ab","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-125","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Okafor is an ornithologist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Okafor measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Okafor found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Okafor concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Okafor found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Okafor concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Okafor measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Because species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings, Okafor concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.1cbc626e79","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-126","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Delacroix is a public health researcher.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Delacroix counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Delacroix found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","To investigate the question, Delacroix counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Because cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year, Delacroix concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Delacroix concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.ca27427e67","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-143","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Castellano is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Castellano scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Castellano found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Castellano concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","To investigate the question, Castellano scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Because regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger, Castellano concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Castellano concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.32ad1b99ba","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-144","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Castellano is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Because kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser, Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.a267c2340c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-147","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Haddad is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Haddad fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Haddad found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Haddad concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Haddad fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Haddad concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Haddad found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","Because kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser, Haddad concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.020ecc1ee4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-153","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Nakamura is a climate scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler, Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","To investigate the question, Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7ca9aceebd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-156","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Takeda is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Takeda moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Takeda found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Takeda concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Takeda concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","To investigate the question, Takeda moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Because fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays, Takeda concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","Takeda found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.1265f37a60","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-172","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Oyelaran is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Oyelaran added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Oyelaran found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Oyelaran added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Oyelaran concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Because the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks, Oyelaran concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Oyelaran found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
